      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why does machine knitting feel so mysterious at first?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Machine knitting involves unfamiliar levers, dials, and settings. Without guidance, it’s hard to know what’s normal and what’s not — which makes everything feel uncertain at the beginning."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do KBM tools help remove guesswork?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "KBM tools are designed to guide you step-by-step. Calculators handle the math, wizards walk you through shaping, and ANA entries answer the exact questions knitters ask every day."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can my question really inspire a new wizard?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Absolutely. Many KBM tools begin as real questions from knitters. If something feels confusing on your machine, chances are you're not the only one — and that makes it a perfect candidate for a new wizard."
      }
    }
  ]
